---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
const domains = [
  ["compositor", "Wayland protocols, windows, input, outputs, session, tiling and scrolling layouts, animation, rendering and the control socket."],
  ["config", "Desktop preferences, translations, session.json and plugin metadata."],
  ["core", "Small contracts: JSON access, files, processes, listener helpers."],
  ["ctl", "lunadashctl, the control client."],
  ["desktop", "Applications, wallpapers (including the video player), themes, shortcuts and system tools used by the shell."],
  ["service", "Standalone services, including the file chooser portal."],
];
const repositories = [
  ["LunaDash", "https://github.com/LuYishan-4/LunaDash", "The compositor, desktop services, packaging and the pins of the other components."],
  ["LunaDash-Shell", "https://github.com/LunaDashWM/LunaDash-Shell", "The panel, dock, launcher, dashboard, settings, switchers and wallpaper library, written in Slint."],
  ["SlintLu", "https://github.com/LunaDashWM/SlintLu", "Runs Slint shells as Wayland layer-shell windows and provides the desktop services."],
  ["LunaDash-docs", "https://github.com/LunaDashWM/LunaDash-docs", "This website."],
];
---
<DocsLayout title="A place for every feature." section="architecture" summary="How the compositor, the Slint shell and SlintLu fit together, and where each feature lives in the source.">
  <h2 id="runtime">How the desktop fits together</h2>
  <p>The C++20 compositor uses wlroots for Wayland protocols, input and scene rendering, with a C11 core for geometry and rendering helpers. It starts the shell as a separate Wayland client: <a href="../../slintlu/">SlintLu</a> runs the <a href="https://github.com/LunaDashWM/LunaDash-Shell">LunaDash shell</a>, written in Slint. The two talk only through Wayland and the compositor's <a href="../api/">control socket</a>; the compositor links no UI toolkit.</p>
  <p>XWayland starts on demand for X11 applications. Video wallpapers play in <code>mpvpaper</code>, which the compositor starts and keeps below the shell's wallpaper surface.</p>

  <h2 id="repositories">Component repositories</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Repository</th><th scope="col">Contains</th></tr></thead><tbody>{repositories.map(([name, url, text]) => <tr><th scope="row"><a href={url}>{name}</a></th><td>{text}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <p>LunaDash's <code>packaging/shell-revision</code> and <code>packaging/slintlu-revision</code> pin the shell and SlintLu commits that packages, the installer and the NixOS module build together.</p>

  <h2 id="domains">Find the feature you want to change</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Under src/</th><th scope="col">Responsibility</th></tr></thead><tbody>{domains.map(([name, description]) => <tr><th scope="row"><code>{name}/</code></th><td>{description}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <p>Directories use lowercase names. C++ interfaces and implementations sit side by side as PascalCase <code>.hpp</code> and <code>.cpp</code> files in the <code>LunaDash</code> namespace; C functions use the <code>ludash_</code> prefix. Each executable has a small <code>Main.cpp</code>. Window layouts implement one interface (<code>compositor/layout/WindowLayout.hpp</code>): the tiling split tree, the scrolling columns and the free-form stacking layout.</p>
  <p><code>nix/</code> holds the Nix packaging and NixOS module, <code>packaging/arch/</code> the Arch package.</p>

  <h2 id="extend">Add a feature without spreading its details</h2>
  <ol><li>Choose the owning domain and define its interface there.</li><li>Shell behaviour belongs in LunaDash-Shell; a runtime capability the shell lacks belongs in SlintLu as a general feature.</li><li>List new sources in the owning CMake target.</li><li>Update the documentation and this website.</li></ol>

  <div class="doc-callout"><p><strong>LunaDash is a development preview.</strong> Physical GPUs, multiple outputs and some input-method details need testing on real systems. Native plugins remain opt-in and run without a sandbox.</p></div>
  <p>Read the <a href="https://github.com/LuYishan-4/LunaDash/blob/dev/docs/en/ARCHITECTURE.md">technical architecture</a> for ownership details.</p>
</DocsLayout>
